result.summary:
Rung C is right with one fix of the change and corrections, none contested. Both steps do what the report says: the test-first order holds in the worker's transcript, the count stage rerun on base and head gives equal tables and output (80.8 s and 81.0 s), and plain-bounded reductions run at the same instances on the base and the head.

The defect I fixed (804445961c): a generic function named as a value inside a generic declaration whose static parameter has the same name was accepted by the names alone, left uninstantiated, and the compiled run died with NoSuchMethodError. The base did the same; it is row 758's own form and the model's (`rows(rmsn, x)` under the same `nat n`). The repair is in TypeAnalyzer.scala: a function's own static parameter counts as unbound where the environment holds its name for another declaration, and the memo of normalized arrow types keys by static parameters too. The new test failed through the harness on the worker's head and passes after; `ant testQuick` is BUILD SUCCESSFUL on the fix (CompilerJUTest 1584, 0 failures).

No count or distance stage ran after the fix, so the report's tables are those of the worker's head. A scratch audit on the distance driver gave output equal to the worker's stage output with the fix in place.

Corrections (4e2385049f, b976846c41):
- two sentences of the specification and row NEW-C-6: a reference at a type that is no arrow type, as `Any`, is still accepted and dies at run time;
- two expected-failure pairs for defects of the base's code that my programs met (rows NEW-C-7 and NEW-C-8);
- row NEW-C-9: a type error in a reduction's body is reported as the big operator's refusal;
- one comment line removed from the reduction's test, and REPORT.md and record.md brought in line with the fix.

The specification was not built after my two sentences; the gather builds it. SKEPTIC.md is committed at /home/user/fortress-static-argument-inferred/explorations/compile-ladder/rung-static-argument-inferred/SKEPTIC.md.
